## psc/sema/modules/loader.pengu — carga de un módulo con F1 + F2.
##
## `SemaModule` es el bundle que posee todo lo que necesita el checker de un
## archivo: `SourceFile`, `LexResult` y `PsParseResult` (que a su vez posee el
## AST). El `DiagnosticBag` es compartido por el programa para conservar el
## orden de diagnósticos entre módulos.
##
## ## Memoria
## `load_module` devuelve un `SemaModule` owned. `free_module` libera parse,
## lex, fuente y path en ese orden. El bag es prestado y no se libera aquí.

import std.archivum
import std.diagnostic as diag

import psc.source as psource
import psc.lexer_state as psstate
import psc.lexer as pslexer
import psc.token as pstoken
import psc.ast.node as psast
import psc.parse.state as pstate
import psc.parse.api as papi
import psc.sema.diagnostics as sdiag
import psc.sema.names as npool
import psc.sema.annotate as ann

insignia sema_loader_

## Un módulo cargado.
##
## ## Memoria
## Sin `derive Nexus`: `free_module` libera cada campo.
rune SemaModule:
    ## Ruta lógica usada en diagnósticos.
    path as string
    ## Fuente; dueño.
    source as psource.SourceFile
    ## Buffer crudo que `source.text` referencia; dueño real.
    source_text as string
    ## Tokens; dueño.
    lex as psstate.LexResult
    ## Parse result; dueño del AST.
    parse as pstate.PsParseResult
    ## `true` si se leyó y parseó sin errores.
    ok as bool
    ## ID asignado por `SemaProgram` (`-1` al cargar).
    id as int
    ## `true` si es el entry.
    is_entry as bool
    ## `true` si vive bajo `std/`.
    is_std as bool
    ## `NameId` del `insignia` (`-1` si no).
    insignia as int
    ## Profundidad de import (para diagnósticos).
    depth as int
    ## Anotaciones semánticas por nodo.
    annotations as ann.SemaAnnotations
    ## Scope global del módulo (`-1` hasta que el programa lo cree).
    scope as int
    ## `nodo de declaración -> TypeId` para la predeclaración.
    type_ids as map of int to int
    ## Módulo padre si este es un binding `.d.pengu` (`-1` si no).
    companion_for as int

## Libera un módulo.
##
## ## Memoria
## Libera el AST, los tokens, la fuente y el path.
weave free_module with m as ref to SemaModule into void:
    calling ann.free_annotations with (sigil of m->annotations)
    banish m->type_ids
    banish m->parse
    banish m->lex
    banish m->source_text
    banish m->source
    banish m->path

## Carga un archivo desde disco.
##
## Si la lectura falla, emite `E0004` y devuelve un módulo vacío con `ok=false`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve un módulo owned; liberar con `free_module`.
weave load_module with path as string, bag as ref to diag.DiagnosticBag, is_entry as bool, is_std as bool, depth as int into SemaModule:
    var m as maybe string is calling archivum.read_text with path
    if not m.is_present:
        return calling empty_module with path, bag, false, is_entry, is_std, depth
    var text as string is calling npool.copy_string with m.value
    defer banish text
    banish m
    return calling load_text with path, text, bag, true, is_entry, is_std, depth

## Carga un módulo desde texto (para tests/LSP).
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve un módulo owned; liberar con `free_module`.
weave load_text with path as string, text as string, bag as ref to diag.DiagnosticBag, readable as bool, is_entry as bool, is_std as bool, depth as int into SemaModule:
    var owned_path as string is calling npool.copy_string with path
    var owned_text as string is calling npool.copy_string with text
    var src as psource.SourceFile is calling SourceFile.from_text with owned_path, owned_text
    calling bag.add_source with path, (calling src.get_text)
    var kw as pstoken.KeywordTable is calling pstoken.keyword_table_new
    var lopt as psstate.LexOptions is calling psstate.default_lex_options
    var lex as psstate.LexResult is calling pslexer.lex with (sigil of src), bag, (sigil of kw), lopt
    banish kw
    var popt as pstate.PsParseOptions is calling pstate.ps_default_parse_options
    var parse as pstate.PsParseResult is calling papi.ps_parse_file with (sigil of src), bag, (sigil of lex), popt
    var notes as ann.SemaAnnotations is calling ann.new_annotations with (sigil of parse.ast)
    return with path is owned_path, source is src, source_text is owned_text, lex is lex, parse is parse, ok is (readable and parse.ok), id is -1, is_entry is is_entry, is_std is is_std, insignia is -1, depth is depth, annotations is notes, scope is -1, type_ids is map of int to int, companion_for is -1

## Módulo vacío para una lectura fallida.
##
## ## Memoria
## Igual que `load_text` pero sin texto; emite E0004.
weave empty_module with path as string, bag as ref to diag.DiagnosticBag, readable as bool, is_entry as bool, is_std as bool, depth as int into SemaModule:
    var msg as string is "cannot read module '{path}'"
    defer banish msg
    var empty as psource.SourceFile is calling empty_source with path
    calling sdiag.node_error with bag, (sigil of empty), sdiag.CODE_UNDEFINED, 0, 0, msg, "Check the path and the project's src/lib directories.", "The module could not be opened."
    banish empty
    return calling load_text with path, "", bag, false, is_entry, is_std, depth

## Fuente vacía auxiliar para emitir un diagnóstico de lectura.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve una fuente owned; el llamador la libera con `banish`.
weave empty_source with path as string into psource.SourceFile:
    return calling SourceFile.from_text with path, ""

## ¿El módulo tiene AST?
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1).
weave has_ast with m as ref to SemaModule into bool:
    return m->parse.root >= 0
